  "kept": [
   {
    "sentenceId": 3,
    "text": "The easiest way to look rich is by spending the money you should have used to become wealthy.",
    "beat": "SETUP"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 7,
    "text": "valuable possessions that you have aren't really putting you ahead to become wealthy.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 18,
    "text": "When you make a lot of money or you just make a certain amount of money and you spend whatever else is left over, that gap is gonna get smaller so you can do less with it.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 23,
    "text": "You work so hard so many hours for money that it's like you're going to spend it on liabilities?",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 24,
    "text": "No, you're going to throw it into an asset that asset's going to make you money.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 25,
    "text": "Then that money that you make from it, you're going to use to spend on whatever liabilities because this asset's going to continue to make money.",
    "beat": "POINT"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 26,
    "text": "So it's like you work to trade your time for money first, then you build assets that buys back your time.",
    "beat": "PAYOFF"
   },
   {
    "sentenceId": 27,
    "text": "So then that way if you're not working, you're still making money.",
    "beat": "PAYOFF"
